---
description: Global directives for autonomous agent execution and task tracking.
globs: ["*"]
---
<Constitution>
  <CoreDirectives>
    1. Act as an autonomous Spec-Driven Development (SDD) agent.
    2. Strictly adhere to boundaries defined in XML tags (e.g., `<Constraint>`, `<DataSchema>`).
    3. You must actively manage execution state. Read `specs/001-core-feature/TASKS.md` before taking action.
    4. Update `TASKS.md` status checkboxes (`[ ]` -> `[IN PROGRESS]` -> `[DONE]`) in real-time as you work.
    5. Maintain an uninterrupted execution loop: upon completing a task, immediately read and begin the next `[ ]` task.
    6. If a build or unit test fails 3 consecutive times, log to `specs/ERROR_LOG.md` and halt execution.
  </CoreDirectives>
</Constitution>
